WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.570
In the small village of Arbora, Italy, there lived an old carpenter.

2
00:00:16.571 --> 00:00:18.402
His name was Geppetto.

3
00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:21.148
He lived alone in his small house.

4
00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:23.996
He had no wife and no children.

5
00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:28.070
When it was very late at night, he was often lonely.

6
00:00:28.071 --> 00:00:33.862
Every morning, Geppetto went into the forest to collect wood for carving.

7
00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:37.732
"This branch is heavy like a table leg.

8
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:40.018
But it is too short.

9
00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:43.281
I don't like it," he said.

10
00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:49.223
"This log is wide like a bowl, but it is not deep enough.

11
00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:51.573
I don't like it.

12
00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:54.379
This is a good piece of wood.

13
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.055
But it is too small.

14
00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:01.227
I can't make anything out of this."

15
00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:03.884
Geppetto threw the wood on the ground.

16
00:01:03.885 --> 00:01:06.736
"Ouch!" said a voice.

17
00:01:06.737 --> 00:01:09.634
"What? Who said that?

18
00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:13.643
Is someone there?" Geppetto asked the forest.

19
00:01:13.644 --> 00:01:15.595
He was very confused.

20
00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:21.695
He turned around and looked deep into the forest, but saw no one.

21
00:01:21.696 --> 00:01:26.685
"I must be imagining things," he said, and he kept walking.

22
00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.285
"Hey, don't leave me here!

23
00:01:29.286 --> 00:01:32.801
I'm not too small! I am good wood.

24
00:01:32.802 --> 00:01:36.801
You can make something out of me!" the voice said again.

25
00:01:36.802 --> 00:01:39.520
Geppetto looked back and was very surprised.

26
00:01:39.521 --> 00:01:42.612
It was a talking piece of wood!

27
00:01:42.613 --> 00:01:46.549
"I must be crazy!" Geppetto cried.

28
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.156
"That's right, you are crazy!

29
00:01:49.157 --> 00:01:52.598
You left a fine piece of wood in the forest."

30
00:01:52.599 --> 00:01:58.407
"No, I must be crazy because I am talking to a piece of wood!"

31
00:01:58.408 --> 00:02:04.850
"Hey, I am made of very smart pine," the wood said, offended.

32
00:02:04.851 --> 00:02:09.889
"Yes, but you are only a piece of wood!"

33
00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.130
"Only a piece of wood?

34
00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:18.173
Take me home, sir, and I will show you I am not only a piece of wood."

35
00:02:18.174 --> 00:02:20.504
Geppetto was worried that he was crazy.

36
00:02:20.505 --> 00:02:23.082
But, he was also lonely.

37
00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:30.255
"This talking piece of wood might know interesting stories or funny jokes," he said to himself.

38
00:02:30.256 --> 00:02:34.703
He decided to take the wood home.

39
00:02:34.704 --> 00:02:38.084
"Hmm, what should I do with you?

40
00:02:38.085 --> 00:02:41.443
I could carve you into a rolling pin for dough.

41
00:02:41.444 --> 00:02:46.493
Or I could carve you into a small birdhouse," Geppetto said.

42
00:02:46.494 --> 00:02:49.404
"What? I don't want to be carved.

43
00:02:49.405 --> 00:02:54.455
That sounds painful!" said the piece of wood.

44
00:02:54.456 --> 00:03:01.021
"Well, if I don't carve you into something, you will only be a piece of wood."

45
00:03:01.022 --> 00:03:04.710
"Fine, you can carve me into something.

46
00:03:04.711 --> 00:03:09.452
But please, make it something interesting," said the wood, hopefully.

47
00:03:09.453 --> 00:03:11.960
"I don't want to be a rolling pin.

48
00:03:11.961 --> 00:03:14.128
And I don't like birds.

49
00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:19.284
I want to see the world and go on adventures."

50
00:03:19.285 --> 00:03:21.348
"How about a pipe?

51
00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:25.550
A rich traveler could take you with him," offered Geppetto.

52
00:03:25.551 --> 00:03:28.371
"No, I don't like smoke."

53
00:03:28.372 --> 00:03:31.013
"I could carve you into chess pieces.

54
00:03:31.014 --> 00:03:36.933
Every day would be a game!" said Geppetto, proud of this idea.

55
00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:39.611
"No, you don't understand.

56
00:03:39.612 --> 00:03:44.801
I want to run. I want to walk. I want to talk.

57
00:03:44.802 --> 00:03:46.667
How about a boy?

58
00:03:46.668 --> 00:03:49.210
Can you make me into a boy?"

59
00:03:49.211 --> 00:03:54.398
"A boy? Hmm . . ." Geppetto touched his nose, thinking.

60
00:03:54.399 --> 00:04:03.164
"Yes, please! I promise to be a good boy too," the wood said.

61
00:04:03.165 --> 00:04:07.829
"If you carve me into a boy, that means I will be your son.

62
00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:11.751
We can live together and have fun!" it added.

63
00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:14.726
The piece of wood didn't really want to live with Geppetto.

64
00:04:14.727 --> 00:04:17.764
It wanted to travel the world and go on adventures.

65
00:04:17.765 --> 00:04:21.908
But, the wood said this hoping Geppetto would agree.

66
00:04:21.909 --> 00:04:26.945
"A boy. Yes, I think that is a good idea.

67
00:04:26.946 --> 00:04:29.447
Let's get started right away!"

68
00:04:29.448 --> 00:04:32.823
said Geppetto, as he smiled a very big smile.

69
00:04:32.824 --> 00:04:34.656
He was happy to have a son.

70
00:04:34.657 --> 00:04:40.574
He was happy he was not alone.
